Patch T7 eng-gpu (rung 1b, task T7): the GPU layer, with the unprotected
half of the libm fix. No path in it is protected. It goes into the same
commit as t7-libm.patch, applied after it.

- crates/eng-gpu: the adapter, the capability report, the fixed render
  graph, offscreen targets, readback, and the shader test
  (tests/shaders.rs, which t7-oracles.patch protects later).
- Cargo.toml `[workspace.dependencies]`: wgpu =30.0.1 with plan decision
  5's features, naga =30.0.1 for the shader test, and libm's
  `force-soft-floats` (t7-libm.patch says why).
- Cargo.lock: the wgpu part of crate batch 2, at the versions of plan.md's
  table (`log`, `ordered-float` and `unicode-width` held at 0.4.34, 5.5.0
  and 0.2.2).
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md: "The GPU layer", eng-gpu no longer a skeleton, and
  how libm's `arch` code stays off, which AGENTS.md and eng-math's crate
  docs now say too.

`cargo deny check` also needs the G3 patch (wgpu's crates on the
allow-list). Base: main at 31c3a8c. At the repo root, after
t7-libm.patch, run `git apply` with this file, then `cargo xtask quick`.
Session 17's T7 entry in PROGRESS.md says how it was tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index bbb22c10aac52cb96c0f97dc49f43a36daa55df8..4524969499938b97adfb4986527ca3ea9d576793 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -46,7 +46,8 @@ seed, tick, last log lines).
 The simulation must give bit-identical results on every OS and CPU.
 
 - Core crates are `#![no_std]` and `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`. Their only
-  third-party dependency is `libm` (pinned `=0.2.16`, `arch` off).
+  third-party dependency is `libm` (pinned `=0.2.16`; `force-soft-floats`
+  keeps its `arch` code off).
 - Math comes from `eng-math` only: `eng_math::{sqrt, sin, min, max, clamp, ...}`.
   Never std float functions, `mul_add`, `algebraic_*`, `to_radians`, or
   approximate SIMD reciprocals. Clippy denies them (`clippy.toml`).
